AB  - Instruments are crucial in industrial monitoring scenarios such as substations and factories. However, their automatic detection remains challenging due to three key issues: (1) the wide variation in instrument shapes, sizes, and display forms reduces the adaptability of general detector; (2) the complex background of industrial scenes inhibits the feature learning of instrument targets; (3) the limited scale and single scene coverage of existing public datasets restrict the generalization ability and fair comparison of algorithms. To address these challenges, this study proposes an efficient instrument detection framework and constructs and publicly releases a large-scale industrial instrument dataset. First, we design a Hierarchical Residual Context Module that captures hierarchical context information through residual connections. This enhances the adaptability of the detector to instruments of different shapes and scales. Second, Gated Compact Convolution is designed based on lightweight convolution and adopts a gating mechanism to focus on key instrument features while compressing parameters through a bottleneck structure. Finally, we designed a Dynamic Threshold Focused Loss: This loss dynamically adjusts weights to suppress susceptible background samples and pay more attention to instrument targets. Experimental results on the industrial instrument dataset show that the proposed framework outperforms the baseline by 3.0% in recall, 4.5% in precision, 1.7% in Mean Average Precision50, and 1.7% in Mean Average Precision50:90. In addition, our instrument detection Visual Internet of Things system, deployed in the field, has demonstrated outstanding performance. Code and dataset are available at https://github.com/dengdengdenggoo/IDYOLO-and-IM-dataset.
