AB  - The Complex Linear Diophantine Fuzzy Set (CLDFS) is one of the latest extensions of fuzzy sets for addressing the ambiguity and uncertainty prevailing in real-world decision-making problems. The range of CLDFS extends to a unit disc in the complex plane rather than the unit interval [0, 1], demonstrating the versatility of this fuzzy extension. On the other hand, the Aczel-Alsina aggregation operator (AAAO) is more versatile and robust in the aggregation process due to its inherent flexibility compared to the other aggregation operators. Considering the benefits of CLDFS as well as AAAO, this study introduces a novel class of aggregation operators to calculate and compile the data's objective uncertainty information. The operators are rigorously examined with respect to essential operational properties and tailored score and accuracy functions to enhance the evaluation and ranking of complex fuzzy data. To validate its effectiveness, a decision-making strategy for sustainable urban drainage systems (SUDS) in Agartala City, Tripura, India, has been planned and verified by the proposed operator. The analysis incorporates three experts from diverse research fields, fourteen criteria and five alternatives. This strategy identified “Flood Prevention and Control” as the most important criterion and “Rainwater Harvesting” as the appropriate technique for the improvement of SUDS of Agartala City. Moreover, parameter exploration and comparison analysis are carried out to suggest the viability and efficacy of the developed procedures. From the analysis, it is clear that the proposed methodology can model the real-world decision-making problems more accurately than its competitors.
