KW  - Missing data generation
KW  - Stochastic degradation modeling
KW  - Interactive prognosis
KW  - Weighted k-nearest neighbors
KW  - Remaining useful life
AB  - Due to sensor performance degradation, network congestion during data transmission, and human factors, the obtained condition monitoring data have the typical issue of data missing, which directly affects the accuracy of subsequent degradation modeling and remaining useful life (RUL) prediction. Existing deep learning studies typically divides it into two separate steps: missing data generation and stochastic degradation modeling, resulting in a lack of explicit connection between the generated data and degradation modeling. Specifically, the prediction results are insufficient for guiding data generation, which substantially affects the accuracy of RUL predictions. Towards this end, this paper proposes a data-model interactive prognosis framework under data-missing conditions. Firstly, missing data are filled using a weighted k-nearest neighbors algorithm, and the RUL of devices is predicted through a linear stochastic model. An optimal objective function based on the mean square error of RUL prediction is established to construct an interactive prognosis framework for data generation and degradation modeling. Secondly, based on the trained interactive prognosis framework, missing data generation and stochastic degradation modeling are achieved in the absence of complete online data. Simultaneously, the Kalman filter algorithm is employed to facilitate online parameter updating for the degradation model. Finally, case studies based on numerical simulations and lithium batteries are provided to verify the effectiveness of the proposed method. The validation results show that the R-squared values of the proposed method are no less than 0.99, indicating high prediction accuracy and potential application value compared with some existing methods.
ER  - 

